{
  "id": "3nkEfr1W",
  "name": "Module depth from the code",
  "summary": "Measures and the gate judge module depth from the code: exposed values, pass-throughs, unused exports, repeated caller math and shallow modules, with no score.",
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "lifecycle": "draft",
  "createdAt": "2026-11-18T21:30:08.571Z",
  "predecessor": "1wIcvaUQ",
  "predecessorRevision": "7836fdce2590e9d0e643b73241a1493779857b1073e9c2cdec07c2a5534160bf",
  "baseline": "38dcee803a0191e0f1edfba164eecdb77f6eb5a3",
  "changes": [
    {
      "type": "assign",
      "subject": "vKEsyHFk/0T9enjhi#AJGft3Pe",
      "field": "description",
      "value": "Its policy also holds whether plain archboard check fails on shallow modules, so that CI and agent loops share one gate. The canonical reader carries it in each model's policy."
    },
    {
      "type": "assign",
      "subject": "vKEsyHFk/XppR9owz#yQCdykGt",
      "field": "description",
      "value": "With --fail-shallow-modules, or when the selected model's policy turns the gate on, it promotes MODULE_SHALLOW on the modules that the branch touched to a warning before the existing exit rule. --base names the branch base; without it the default-base lookup decides. A base that does not resolve is a refusal, never a pass."
    },
    {
      "type": "assign",
      "subject": "vKEsyHFk/HBlhIeSD#yYQ3AHkf",
      "field": "description",
      "value": "Per model, state and revision it keeps each module's exports, counts, findings, language coverage and skipped reads, modules with no findings included, so a pane tells a clean result from an incomplete read."
    },
    {
      "type": "assign",
      "subject": "vKEsyHFk/HBlhIeSD#radK8osF",
      "field": "description",
      "value": "The branch footprint can read the working tree as its head, so a gate run before a commit sees what the branch changed."
    },
    {
      "type": "assign",
      "subject": "vKEsyHFk/HBlhIeSD#5SMX69gS",
      "field": "description",
      "value": "The checker reads current architecture, one selected state, or independent drafts. It reports bindings, anchors, declared relationships, interfaces, module depth and document references with canonical identities. It reads the interface of every bound module, with or without parts, in every language that the module holds, and hands Module depth what it read. EXPOSED_UNUSED is a warning when the reader resolved every use in that language and the model draws no outside caller of the entry; otherwise it is information. The answer marks the modules that the branch touched and carries the selected model's shallow-module setting; severities in the answer never depend on the caller's flags. Its state reader also reads one selected state at a source ref, through the branch reading, for the branch footprint of a named head. Git locality and branch footprint use separate requested history operations. The timings of its language servers name the program that ran and the TypeScript that it read."
    },
